From 0b24b61e2fe59775cc0076167a1d2e022fca70a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ALH477 <demodllc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:40:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] src: font tests must skip loudly, not pass silently

Five tests open a system font with `catch return`. A bare `return` from a
test body reports as a PASS, so on any machine without these exact paths
the suite is green while asserting nothing -- including an Arch box that
simply lacks ttf-liberation or ttf-iosevka-term-nerd.

    src/type.zig            "glyph and layout from system font"
                            "color emoji glyph"
                            "bold face is a different glyph"
    src/type/truetype.zig   "rasterize system font"
    src/type/cbdt.zig       "noto color emoji grin"

Route them through a small helper that returns error.SkipZigTest and
prints the path instead. The test runner counts skips separately, so the
result is honest either way. A failure *after* a successful open stays a
real error rather than a skip.

    before:  96/96 tests passed          (5 of them asserting nothing)
    after:   91 pass, 5 skip (96 total)  (each skip printed by path)
